# Staging & releases

## Branches

- **`staging`** — default integration branch. Day-to-day work merges here first.
- **`main`** — production (viselle.net / production Vercel). Promote only via staging → main when cutting a release.

No force-push to `main`.

## Semver (start at 0.0.1)

When promoting staging → main, bump **one** of:

| Part | Meaning |
|------|---------|
| **z (patch)** | User won’t notice unless a bug affects them |
| **y (minor)** | User will notice; no retraining / no breaking change |
| **x (major)** | Breaks compatibility or requires user retraining |

Phases: **alpha** (0.x) → **beta** (3-month trials) → **GA** (1.0.0+).

## Release notes

Public page: `/releases` (no auth). Source of truth: `CHANGELOG.md` (also rendered via `src/content/releases.md`). Keep them in sync when cutting a release. Link lives in the marketing footer.

## Release cut (required for every staging → main)

Never merge `staging` → `main` without bumping. Use:

`npm run cut-release -- --bump patch|minor|major` (or on Windows: `node scripts/cut-release.mjs --bump=patch`).

The script auto-gathers commit subjects since the last `vX.Y.Z` tag (or `origin/main`), writes VERSION / package.json / CHANGELOG / `src/content/releases.md`, and (when the sibling API repo is present) includes API commits under an **API** section. Preview with `--dry-run`. Bump **both** this repo and Beauty-Backend-API to the same version, then merge, tag `vX.Y.Z`, and deploy.

## Environments (separate DBs)

Staging frontend (Vercel `staging` branch) must point `VITE_API_BASE_URL` at the **staging API**, which uses a **separate Supabase project** from production. Never point staging UI at production API/DB for day-to-day testing that mutates data.
